1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,387
The History of the Handshake.

2
00:00:02,337 --> 00:00:09,075
The handshake originated in ancient Greece as a peace gesture, demonstrating that the right hand held no weapon.

3
00:00:09,075 --> 00:00:13,950
Romans adapted this into a forearm grasp to check for concealed daggers.

4
00:00:13,950 --> 00:00:20,575
The modern handshake standardized in 19th-century Europe as a single vertical clasp with pumping motion.

5
00:00:20,575 --> 00:00:27,325
Customs vary globally: Japan prefers bowing; Thailand uses the wai (pressed palms with a slight bow).

6
00:00:27,325 --> 00:00:34,037
The COVID-19 pandemic prompted a temporary shift toward elbow bumps and nods in professional settings.

7
00:00:34,037 --> 00:00:47,025
This 2,500-year tradition illustrates how a physical act carries deep cultural meaning across civilizations, reflecting values of trust, equality, and mutual respect in social interaction.

